 generate shapes unconditionally, PVD completes (or inpaints) full shapes when a partial point cloud is fixed during inference. For general diffusion models, Song et al. (2021) proposed an alternative inpainting approach and remarked that this approach produces approximate conditional samples. However, these methods do not provide theoretical guarantees, and when we compare them to SMCDiff, we find that their approximation error impedes performance when applied to motifscaffolding. Saharia et al. (2021) developed an inpainting diffusion model by training a diffusion model to denoise randomly generated masked regions while unmasked regions were unperturbed. However, their approach requires a detailed data augmentation strategy that does not exist for proteins.\nWe describe additional related work on protein generative models in Appendix A."
